WEBVTT - observer: who watches which log

NOTE
One cue per item, one second long, in the order the items were settled; the time is the order, not a clock. The identifier names the item; the text says what it is, when, and where it lives. A cue that is replaced is not deleted: a later cue says what replaced it. Here each cue registers an observer: its identifier is the observer, its text what it watches and when.

claude
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Observes global.vtt and environment.vtt: read before acting, so settled decisions are not asked again.

production-observes-development
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.000
When a development cue writes into ZIGUAROTH, a production cue records the placement.

global-observes-all
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.000
When a cue anywhere records a decision by the author, global.vtt gets the decision as its own cue.

author
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Observes production.vtt: what is placed, and what is waiting for a decision or a commit.

codex
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Codex: the author hands it briefs. The WSN brief it receives says OMI.WSN already exists (parse, render, accepts, expanded, cast) under types/AGENTS.md's rules, and carries the corrections: no Name decided by a prefix, two readings of ADONAI, no self-referencing WORD production, nothing settled on which form is stronger.

forwarded-replies
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Other assistants' replies the author forwards are read as claims and tested against the code, the spec or Plan 9 before anything is built on them.
